# The M1a demo, as fans do it (docs/demos/m1a.md). Start the AppHost in demo mode
# (dotnet run --project dev/AppHost -- --Demo=true) and start the "seed" resource first.
# Run the requests top to bottom: each one uses values from the ones before.
# Fans: ana, ben, cid, dan, eva, fil; passwords equal the names. Tokens last 5 minutes.

@publicApi = http://localhost:5101
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180

### Step 3. Browse: published events that haven't started, soonest first (no sign-in needed)
GET {{publicApi}}/events

### Search event and venue names (web search syntax: "quoted phrase", -excluded)
# @name list
GET {{publicApi}}/events?q=demo concert&pageSize=1

### Event page: venue, prices, sales phase, seat-map URL
# @name page
GET {{publicApi}}/events/{{list.response.body.$.items[0].eventId}}

### Seat map, at the versioned URL from the event page (cached for good)
GET {{publicApi}}{{page.response.body.$.seatMapUrl}}

### What's free: places per section, and the free seats (the client joins them with the seat map on seatId)
# @name availability
GET {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/availability

### Step 4. Sign in as ana (password grant, development client only)
# @name ana
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=ana&password=ana

### Ana holds two seats: 201, all or none. For the best free places instead: { "section": "A", "quantity": 2 }
# @name hold
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[0]}}", "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[1]}}" ] }

### Sign in as ben
# @name ben
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=ben&password=ben

### Ben tries the same seats: 409, at once
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{ben.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[0]}}", "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[1]}}" ] }

### Step 5. Ana checks out: open redirectUrl in a browser and click Approve
# @name order
POST {{publicApi}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holdId": "{{hold.response.body.$.holdId}}" }

### Ana's order: Pending until LocalPay's webhook confirms it (what the return page polls)
GET {{publicApi}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}

### (Changed your mind before checkout? Release a hold; one hold per fan per event)
DELETE {{publicApi}}/holds/{{hold.response.body.$.holdId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Step 7a. Sign in as cid
# @name cid
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=cid&password=cid

### Cid holds a seat (note expiresAt: a minute in demo mode), then walks away
# @name cidHold
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{cid.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[2]}}" ] }

### Sign in as dan
# @name dan
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=dan&password=dan

### Dan holds the same seat: 409 until Cid's hold expires, 201 the moment it does
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{dan.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[2]}}" ] }

### Step 7b. Sign in as eva
# @name eva
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=eva&password=eva

### Eva holds a seat
# @name evaHold
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{page.response.body.$.eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{eva.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "seatIds": [ "{{availability.response.body.$.availableSeatIds[3]}}" ] }

### Eva checks out and walks away (don't open the payment page)
# @name evaOrder
POST {{publicApi}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{eva.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holdId": "{{evaHold.response.body.$.holdId}}" }

### Two minutes later: Expired. Open her redirectUrl: LocalPay says expired. The seat is free again.
GET {{publicApi}}/orders/{{evaOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{eva.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Step 8. The Failure Scenarios event: hold ONE seat; its price picks LocalPay's scenario
# @name scenarios
GET {{publicApi}}/events?q=failure scenarios&pageSize=1

### Sign in as fil
# @name fil
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/eventticketing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=eventticketing-dev&username=fil&password=fil

### Fil holds the best seat in section A (rows 1-10 cost 25.03: the webhook comes twice).
### Other sections: B completes during expiry, C is declined, D's webhook is late.
# @name filHold
POST {{publicApi}}/events/{{scenarios.response.body.$.items[0].eventId}}/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{fil.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "section": "A", "quantity": 1 }

### Fil checks out: approve on LocalPay's page; the order is confirmed once despite two webhooks
# @name filOrder
POST {{publicApi}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{fil.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holdId": "{{filHold.response.body.$.holdId}}" }

### Fil's order
GET {{publicApi}}/orders/{{filOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fil.response.body.$.access_token}}
